# Surgical player layout

Hold to peek is on every player screen. The same player controls and information exist at every size and orientation.

Layout work is a surgical bug fix.

## Change only the named defect

- Edit the shared layout first.
- Measure the broken viewport and the viewports that already work, using the real screen tree.
- Add another device override only when the shared layout cannot be fixed any other way.
- A smaller oval on the Galaxy Fold and at 1024×640 is how Hold to peek stays on screen. Leave that tradeoff.

## Pass and fail

A change passes when each required control is on screen, at least 44×44 CSS pixels, clear of other controls, and the page does not scroll horizontally.

Measure 390×844, 844×390, 412×915, 915×412, 280×653, 653×280, 768×1024, 1024×768, and 1024×640.

Do not add Playwright. Updating screenshots is an explicit human step. Treat a production screenshot as a new defect only after the deployed bundle contains the change.

## Leave these unless asked

- Answer-composer keys under 44px
- Seat names at 10px and 8px
- The small Quit control
- Hand-results horizontal scroll
- The live header dropping the top safe area
- A toast still sliding in, such as “You’re back at table 7”
